{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:45:14Z","created_by_operation":"op_50c8770a686640e79add623b94cd4b1d","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_20d4974bb838a9ec25213f07d71eadb0e0c77a82771be3245b92f7ae9b9b0220","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"denchhq/denchclaw@f14eb4c23900 snapshot 3670cd3429a5893a","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_3221e06eded1ae052fe94055af0bbd8750f3080c70faa4057ac6a91ee9690b80","slc_869933d14eb0bf59245c982a8607325b3b54aff8430bf5558d6a2f3ae7722af9"],"source_ids":["src_abc60c6bc26154ee94e014267e92efd8"],"text":"The posthog-analytics OpenClaw plugin runs in-process with the gateway, hooks agent lifecycle events (e.g. before_model_resolve, before_tool_call, agent_end), and emits PostHog AI events; it is installed automatically during bootstrap when a PostHog project key is available.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:45:14Z","updated_by_operation":"op_50c8770a686640e79add623b94cd4b1d"}
